<GuideLayout 
  title="Understanding Global Activewear Quality Standards: ISO, SGS & BSCI" 
  type="COMPLIANCE"
  description="A guide to the certifications that matter. Learn how ISO and SGS standards protect your brand's reputation and ensure product safety."
>
  <h2>Why Certifications Matter</h2>
  <p>In the global B2B market, certifications are the language of trust. They prove that a factory operates under strict quality management and ethical standards.</p>
  
  <h3>ISO 9001: Quality Management</h3>
  <p>This is the baseline for any professional factory. It ensures that the manufacturer has a consistent system for monitoring production, managing documentation, and correcting errors.</p>

  <h3>SGS: Third-Party Validation</h3>
  <p>SGS is the world's leading inspection and testing company. An SGS report validates that the fabrics we use meet specific technical requirements—such as colorfastness, shrinkage limits, and tensile strength.</p>

  <h3>BSCI: Ethical Manufacturing</h3>
  <p>The Business Social Compliance Initiative (BSCI) ensures that your products are made in a socially responsible way, with fair wages, safe working conditions, and no child labor.</p>

  <h3>Fitclo's Commitment</h3>
  <p>At Fitclo, we maintain a 100% compliance record. We invite our clients to request copies of our latest audit reports and fabric testing results before placing their bulk orders.</p>
</GuideLayout>
